anv: AV1 encode BRC picks the CDEF parameters (Xe2)

With CDEF enabled in the sequence header (FFmpeg 0001: under rate control, as with VAAPI), media-driver lets the
HuC BRC update kernel choose the CDEF parameters (Av1Brc: UPD_EnableCDEFUpdate when enable_cdef and not intra block
copy) and reads them back from the output AVP_INLOOP_FILTER_STATE (DW5: cdef_bits 29:28). cdef_params() is
4 + 12 << cdef_bits bits (5.9.19), so with the kernel's choice the frame header has one of 4 lengths per loop filter
variant of 0016: pack all (up to 8), capture DW5 next to the loop filter levels, and run the padding / tile group
header / leb128 sub-batch whose loop filter and cdef_bits checks (MI_CONDITIONAL_BATCH_BUFFER_END) both hold.

